.TITLE "ssh"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Securely logs into a remote machine and executes commands. It is the industry standard for __remote administration__ and encrypted communication over unsecured networks.

.DIV "TLDR"
**ssh user@host**
Connects to a remote server using the specified username and hostname or IP address.
> __user@host__ remote identity

**ssh -p port user@host**
Connects to a remote server using a non-standard port.
> __-p__ port flag | __port__ the numeric port | __user@host__ remote identity

**ssh -i key_file user@host**
Uses a specific private key file for authentication instead of a password.
> __-i__ identity file flag | __key_file__ path to the private key

**ssh user@host "command"**
Executes a single command on the remote server and then closes the connection.
> __user@host__ identity | __"command"__ the remote command to run

.DIV "SUMMARY"
For a more convenient experience, you can use __ssh-copy-id__ to transfer your public key to a server, allowing you to log in without a password. Always protect your private keys and never share them with anyone.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:scp** **cli:ssh-keygen** **cli:ssh-agent**

